  "toyota_summary": "The International Maritime Organization began negotiations today on shipping emissions standards, with multiple competing frameworks now on the table. China has tabled a specific proposal aimed at finding middle ground between the diverging camps, signaling it may play kingmaker in talks that will determine how much it costs to move vehicles by sea over the next decade.\n\nShipping decarbonization rules will reshape logistics costs for automakers moving finished vehicles and parts globally. A strict standard could add hundreds of dollars per car to transport expenses; a weak one invites carbon tariffs from Europe and pressure from investors. The outcome will likely influence which regions become more or less attractive for manufacturing and distribution.\n\nWatch whether the U.S. and EU can align on a baseline before the IMO settles this week.",
